Several case studies illustrate the impact of antitrust laws on market competition. For example, the Microsoft antitrust case in the US, where the company was found guilty of violating antitrust laws by bundling its web browser with its operating system, demonstrates the importance of enforcing antitrust laws to prevent dominant companies from abusing their market power. In China, the Qualcomm antitrust case, where the company was fined for engaging in anti-competitive practices in the mobile chip market, shows the growing efforts of Chinese authorities to enforce antitrust laws and promote competition.

